<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Wellness and Mindfulness</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How Exercise Helps My Body</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Reading: Outline the main information from simple diagrams (e.g., graphs, bar charts). Reading: Recognize the language on a simple form asking for personal information.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can outline key points from bar charts on fitness benefits and connect them to physical education and extracurricular activities (e.g., "List two main benefits of regular exercise for students who participate in physical education or extracurricular activities like baseball, soccer, volleyball, and folkloric dance.")
Can recognize the language used on wellness questionnaires (e.g., "On the health check-in form, I need to fill out my name, age, and how many hours I sleep each night.")
Can outline information from graphs on stress-reduction techniques (e.g., "The graph indicates that deep breathing techniques are the most commonly used method by students to reduce stress, followed by meditation and exercise.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; width: 45%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a series of images showing different forms of exercise (e.g., running, stretching, meditating, playing soccer). Students briefly name the activity and, in one or two words, state a physical or mental benefit they remember from Lesson 1. For example, "Running - energy boost!" or "Stretching - flexibility." This activates prior vocabulary and connects to the theme "How Exercise Helps My Body."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key multisyllabic vocabulary related to wellness and exercise, focusing on word stress: "flexi<b>bi</b>lity," "re<b>si</b>lience," "mindful<b>ness</b>." The teacher then uses minimal pair drills for /ʊ/ and /uː/ by saying pairs like "could" /kʊd/ and "cooed" /kuːd/, "soot" /sʊt/ and "suit" /suːt/, ensuring students hear the distinction. Example sentence: "He <b>could</b> wear a <b>suit</b> to the meeting." The teacher then demonstrates the activity of outlining key information by quickly looking at a simple visual aid (e.g., a simple chart showing "Favorite Sports") and pointing out its main title and categories.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'flexibility' mean? Can you show me an example with your body?" (Checks understanding of key vocabulary).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a graph shows 'hours of sleep,' what kind of information will it give us?" (Checks understanding of outlining information from diagrams).</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students receive a handout with three integrated parts:
                <ol style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A short article titled "The Power of Movement: How Exercise Benefits Your Body and Mind," featuring vocabulary like <em>wellness, energy, benefits, strength, flexibility, mental well-being, promote, enhance</em>.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A simple bar chart illustrating "Top 4 Benefits of Regular Exercise for Teenagers" (e.g., Boosts Energy, Improves Focus, Reduces Stress, Strengthens Body), using the vocabulary <em>energy, focus, strength</em>.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">An excerpt from a "Daily Wellness Check-in Form" asking for basic personal information (Name, Age, Hours of Sleep Last Night, Today's Mood [e.g., Calm, Energized]) to recognize language for forms.</li>
                </ol>
                Genre: Informative article, bar chart/infographic, simple questionnaire. Register: Neutral/Informal. Format: Printed handout.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading: Comprehend simple, direct factual texts on familiar topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions:</b> Students read the article and answer: "What is the main idea of 'The Power of Movement' article?" (e.g., Exercise helps our body and mind).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read specific sentences about the bar chart and decide if they are true or false based on the data. E.g., "According to the bar chart, 'Reduces Stress' is the top benefit."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match sections of the "Daily Wellness Check-in Form" to the type of information requested. E.g., "Name" -> "Personal identification."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading for specific details and outlining information. Using Present Simple for general statements about benefits (e.g., "Exercise boosts energy.") and collocations (e.g., "improve strength," "promote wellness"). Focus on vocabulary: <em>exercise, benefits, strength, flexibility, mental well-being, routine, meditate, boost, improve, relax, promote, physical, healthy, strong, flexible, mindful, energized, balanced, calm</em>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Fill-in-the-blanks):</b> Students read incomplete sentences related to the article and fill in the blanks using target vocabulary provided in a word bank (e.g., <em>wellness, improve, balance, mindful, strength</em>). Example: "Regular exercise can help _______ your mental well-being and ______ your physical ________."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Diagram Interpretation):</b> Students work individually to complete sentences describing the information presented in the bar chart. Example stems: "The chart indicates that the most common benefit of exercise is ________." or "Students can _______ their body by practicing regular exercise, which also ________ their focus." Students then identify three pieces of information they would expect to see on a *complete* wellness questionnaire, based on the excerpt.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Peer Check & Discussion):</b> In pairs, students compare their answers for the fill-in-the-blanks and diagram interpretation tasks. They discuss which exercise benefit is most important for their own <em>routine</em> or <em>habit</em> and why, using phrases like "I think [benefit] is important because..." or "Some people like to [verb] because it helps them [verb] stress." They also share one personal wellness practice (e.g., "I exercise three times a week to stay fit and focused," "I am practicing mindfulness to relax.")</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a new, simple graph or bar chart (e.g., "Common Stress-Reduction Techniques Used by 9th Graders" or "Preferred Extracurricular Physical Activities"). This graph will contain vocabulary like <em>meditation, relaxation, exercise, deep breathing, focus</em>.
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Reading and Outlining. Each group's task is to read and outline the main information from their assigned graph. They must identify the title, the categories, and the key findings. For example, "The graph indicates that deep breathing techniques are the most commonly used method by students to reduce stress, followed by meditation and exercise."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> The graphs are related to wellness, mindfulness, and physical activity, directly linking to "How Exercise Helps My Body" and student experiences.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in interpreting visual data, collaboration in outlining, and using target vocabulary (<em>boost, improve, strengthen, relax, meditate, promote, balance, enhance, maintain, focus</em>) and grammar (Present Simple) to summarize findings. They will engage in group discussions on wellness routines, contributing suggestions and solutions to promote mental and physical well-being by interpreting the data.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment. The teacher circulates, observing each group's collaboration and their outlined information. Peers provide feedback on the clarity and completeness of other groups' outlines.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group verbally presents their outlined information from their assigned graph to the class (1-2 minutes per group). They should clearly state the main findings, using vocabulary from the lesson and present simple tense. For example: "Our graph shows that playing soccer is the most popular activity, promoting both strength and endurance."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of key vocabulary (e.g., "flexibility," "resilience").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of target vocabulary (e.g., <em>benefits, strength, mental well-being, relax</em>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and accuracy in outlining the main information from the graph.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Evidence of collaborative interaction within the group.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on an index card before leaving:
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I learned how to outline information from _______ and recognized language on a ________."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One benefit of exercise that surprised me in the readings was ________."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of reading and outlining information from graphs was most challenging for me today, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can the information I outlined today help me make healthier choices about my own wellness routine?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well in terms of engaging students with the reading materials and diagrams? Students were able to outline key information from charts, demonstrating strong comprehension. The pair work and group activity for diagram interpretation fostered collaboration and effective use of target vocabulary. What adjustments are needed for the next lesson? Some students struggled with distinguishing long and short vowels; a quick review using new minimal pairs might be beneficial. Ensure more specific prompts for using present continuous in subsequent speaking tasks. How will this lesson connect to the next lesson? This reading lesson provided a strong foundation of vocabulary and understanding of wellness benefits. The next lesson (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction) will build on this knowledge by having students actively discuss and share their own wellness routines and ideas, using the language practiced today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>